  "body": "As of now `console.dirxml(\"Dom %s\", \"Farolino\", document.createElement('h1'))` will print:\r\n\r\n > Dominic Farolino *\\<h1>*\r\n\r\nin Chrome and Safari though the spec does not account for it. This format specifier substitution does not take place in Firefox, and I'm not sure about Edge's behavior.\r\n\r\nIn the spec I think we should make a call to `Formatter(...` inside `dirxml`, as this functionality exists in at least two browsers. Furthermore it seems that the call to `Formatter(...` must come after we iterate through the *`...data`* transforming DOM elements into their optimal form because `console.dirxml(\"%O\", document.createElement('h1'))` prints the JavaScript object representation of the `h1` element in Chrome and Safari, indicating that the format specifier has the last say.\r\n\r\nIf Edge also includes format specifier behavior, I think we simply file a Firefox bug and add it to the spec.",
